    <DataNode elementId="AT3G44860-MONOMER" textLabel="farnesoic acid carboxyl methyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FYC4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">The farnesoic acid carboxyl methyltransferase (FAMT) identified in |FRAME: ORG-5993| is a member of the plant family of SABBATH methyltransferases |CITS: [16165084]|. &lt;i&gt;In vitro&lt;/i&gt; characterization of this enzyme shows that it can methylate a number of structurally related compounds, but that |FRAME: CPD-12585| is its preferred substrate. Atlhough |FRAME:CPD-12586 &lt;i&gt;E,E&lt;/i&gt;-methyl farnesoate| has not been detected in Arabidopsis in &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;, it has been observed in other plants where the biological importance of it and related compounds remains to be determined |CITS: [11598232][16165084]|. However, the up-regulation of FAMT transcript levels by a fungal elicitor, as well as treatments with jasmonic acid and salicylic acid, suggest a possible involvement for |FRAME:CPD-12586 &lt;i&gt;E,E&lt;/i&gt;-methyl farnesoate| or structurally similar compounds in plant defense |CITS: [16165084]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G44860-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G44860.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9FYC4" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33368, RXN-18064" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G44860.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G44860" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Species" value="ORG-5993" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16165084" />
    </DataNode>
